.TH COMM 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
comm \- select or reject lines common to two files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B comm
.RB [ \-123 ]
.I file1
.I file2
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B comm
reads
.I file1
and
.IR file2 ,
which must already be sorted in byte-collating order, and writes a
merged listing of their lines in up to three columns, separated by a
single <tab> character:
.RS
.TP
.B 1
lines only in
.IR file1 ;
.TP
.B 2
lines only in
.IR file2 ;
.TP
.B 3
lines in both files.
.RE
.PP
Column 1 never has a leading <tab>. Column 2 is preceded by one <tab>
for each of the columns before it (0 or 1) that is still being shown.
Column 3 is preceded by one <tab> for each of the columns before it
(0, 1, or 2) that is still being shown.
.PP
.B comm
never sorts its input, and does not check that either file is
actually sorted; if an input is not sorted, the output is undefined.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-1
Suppress column 1 (lines only in
.IR file1 ).
.TP
.B \-2
Suppress column 2 (lines only in
.IR file2 ).
.TP
.B \-3
Suppress column 3 (lines in both files).
These may be combined in one option, such as
.BR \-12 ,
or given separately.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I file1
The pathname of the first file to compare. If given as
.BR \- ,
standard input is used.
.TP
.I file2
The pathname of the second file to compare. If given as
.BR \- ,
standard input is used.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Both input files were read and compared successfully.
.TP
.B >0
An error occurred: an invalid option, a missing or extra operand, or
an unreadable input file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sort (1),
.BR uniq (1),
.BR diff (1),
.BR join (1)
